 "id": "01a10809-56e3-7fb1-8685-b514743b5329",
 "summary": "Invoice PDFs render via WeasyPrint in src/billing/pdf.py; font set in code via @font-face (Inter)",
 "content": "Invoice PDFs are rendered by `render_pdf()` in src/billing/pdf.py with WeasyPrint (v2 renderer, gated by the `invoice-pdf-v2` flag, which is on in flags.toml; the old wkhtmltopdf/pdfkit path was removed). The font is set in code: the module-level `_STYLE` CSS declares `@font-face { font-family: Inter; src: url(assets/Inter.woff2) }` and `body { font-family: Inter }`, using a shared `FontConfiguration`. Font problems are therefore code/asset problems, not Dockerfile/fontconfig problems. Note: the URL is relative and the CSS/HTML are built from strings with no base_url, and as of 2026-10-04 no Inter.woff2 exists in the repo, so WeasyPrint silently falls back to a system font.",
 "clear_validity": true,
 "physical": [
  "src/billing/pdf.py",
  "flags.toml"
 ]
}
